{"content": "The release codename mentioned in the comment is **COBALT-PELICAN-5104**.\n\nThe first class defined in the excerpt, `PurePath`, serves as a base class for manipulating filesystem paths without performing any actual I/O operations. It provides a unified interface for handling path components (like drive, root, and tail) and offers methods for path arithmetic, normalization, and pattern matching that work across different operating systems (POSIX and Windows) by delegating specific behaviors to subclasses like `PurePosixPath` and `PureWindowsPath`.", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6074694956997817, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6074694956997817}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -0.9513339366177505}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -3.33356278793611}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -4.076406415865797}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -4.914379056857008}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -5.2732638682583755}, {"token": "First", "logprob": -5.737672742770094}, {"token": "-", "logprob": -8.900705274508375}, {"token": "Release", "logprob": -9.04281800644197}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -9.93374246017732}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -10.011936124728102}, {"token": "Answer", "logprob": -10.597068723605055}, {"token": "based", "logprob": -10.624746259615797}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -10.674995359347243}, {"token": "What", "logprob": -10.786792692110915}, {"token": "Hello", "logprob": -10.991446432040114}, {"token": "```", "logprob": -11.372702535555739}, {"token": "*", "logprob": -11.40596383468904}, {"token": "Third", "logprob": -11.409933027193922}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -11.463480886385817}]}, {"token": " release", "logprob": -0.00018204811377842134, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " release", "logprob": -0.00018204811377842134}, {"token": " first", "logprob": -8.8373822129087}, {"token": " code", "logprob": -12.08707703712745}, {"token": " second", "logprob": -12.160954371722177}, {"token": " comment", "logprob": -12.5509556687