{"content": "The release codename mentioned in a comment is **COBALT-PELICAN-5104**.\n\nThe first class defined in the excerpt is `PurePath`, which serves as a base class for representing filesystem paths as data objects without performing any actual system I/O. It provides methods to manipulate, parse, and normalize path components (such as drive, root, and tail) in a way that is agnostic to the operating system's specific file actions, allowing it to act as either a semantic model for paths or a parent for platform-specific subclasses like `PurePosixPath` and `PureWindowsPath`.", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6074694956997817, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6074694956997817}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -0.9513339366177505}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -3.33356278793611}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -4.076406415865797}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -4.914379056857008}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -5.2732638682583755}, {"token": "First", "logprob": -5.737672742770094}, {"token": "-", "logprob": -8.900705274508375}, {"token": "Release", "logprob": -9.04281800644197}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -9.93374246017732}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -10.011936124728102}, {"token": "Answer", "logprob": -10.597068723605055}, {"token": "based", "logprob": -10.624746259615797}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -10.674995359347243}, {"token": "What", "logprob": -10.786792692110915}, {"token": "Hello", "logprob": -10.991446432040114}, {"token": "```", "logprob": -11.372702535555739}, {"token": "*", "logprob": -11.40596383468904}, {"token": "Third", "logprob": -11.409933027193922}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -11.463480886385817}]}, {"token": " release", "logprob": -0.00018204811377842134, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " release", "logprob": -0.00018204811377842134}, {"token": " first", "logprob": -8.8373822129087}, {"token": " code", "logprob": -12.08707703712745}, {"token": " second", "logprob": -12.160954371722177}, {"token": " comment", "logp